+patches/0540: the snapshot strictly before the prompt's end (GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_BEFORE_END, default 1)
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+A resume needs a snapshot of a STRICT prefix (``decode._prefill``: the first token is sampled from the prompt's last
+row, which a snapshot does not hold). Rule 2 put a prompt that ends on the grid (n = kG) at S = n, so an identical
+prompt sent again (a regenerate / retry, an agent resending its context, RigMark's "immediate replay") could not
+resume from it and fell back to the next session mark down (every 16,384 tokens): W13 replays resumed 0 / 16,384 /
+49,152 of 8,192 / 32,768 / 65,536 tokens. With ``before`` (the caller asks for it on the prefill that ends at the
+prompt's end: ``engine._run``, the batcher's last piece), S is the last grid point STRICTLY before n,
+(n - 1) // G * G, for every n, with rule 2's tail exception unchanged; so an on-grid prompt is treated exactly as
+the other G - 1 of every G lengths already were (one cut, snapshot at n - G), and a resend re-prefills at most G rows
+(or tail + G). The snapshot REPLACES the one at n (one per prompt, as before: no extra memory); a next turn that
+extends the prompt resumes G rows earlier than before, on 1 prompt length in G. Exact prefills (grid 0: a snapshot may
+sit anywhere) take theirs at the same S (a cut; exact chunks never depend on their cuts) instead of after the prompt.
+A cut and a snapshot at a multiple of 64 are what every other prompt length already gets: no new arithmetic, resumed
+== fresh as for every snapshot. Cost: one more chunk (one more read of the weights) on a prompt that ends on the grid
+and whose last chunk starts more than ``tail`` rows before S. Both ranks must agree (checked at load, ``engine``).
+
 Nothing here imports torch (the session store and host tests use it).
 """
 
